  "definitions": "Boardings = one passenger getting on a vessel (unlinked); one row per route per calendar day, with trips operated, bike boardings, passenger miles (FAQ).",
  "method": "Downloaded every daily route row for each fiscal year (Jul 1 - Jun 30) from the public API used by the dashboard. avgWeekday = mean of daily boardings over Mon-Fri days the route operated, excluding reduced-service weekdays. Reduced-service weekdays were detected as Mon-Fri dates where Vallejo trips operated < 75% of that FY's median weekday Vallejo trips (catches holidays run on weekend/holiday schedule plus a few disruption days; the list is in reducedServiceWeekdaysExcluded). avgSaturday/avgSunday = mean over Saturdays/Sundays the route operated (holidays falling on weekdays are excluded from all three). The API day-of-week is the calendar day, not the service type. For event routes (OAB, VB, P48, ...) the averages are per operating day, not per calendar weekday. systemAvgWeekday sums all routes on each typical weekday. These are agency daily counts aggregated by this project, not agency-published averages.",
  "crossChecks": [
   "FY2026 system total from API = 3,259,406; WETA press release (blog.bayareametro.gov, Aug 2026) says \"3.25 million passengers from July 2025 through the end of June\". Consistent.",
   "NTD 2024 (other-operators.json) avg typical weekday UPT 6,987 vs this FY2024 systemAvgWeekday 7,204 (NTD uses its own typical-weekday definition); annual NTD 2,388,379 vs API FY2024 2,407,383 (+0.8%; the FAQ says values can be revised).",
   "Widget /api/widgets (accessed 2026-10-04): total_ridership_2019 = 3,215,500 (calendar 2019); last 12 months to August 2026 = 3,307,565."
